invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: check_power runs the check's public operation on rsa_vp1, which
  takes no description of the CPU, where the session's value names AVX-512
  IFMA, so the check runs rsa_mont64.c's loops beside exponentiations on
  the kernel, at several times their cost. The verdict is the same.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into rsa_ifma_public on
  test/rsa_ifma_count.c's stand-in and requires one from each signature
  on the kernels. Only an x86-64 object makes the call, so
  test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds the binary for x86-64; the lane skips
  without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        rsa_vp1_cpu(cpu, k->n, k->n_len, candidate, power);
--- new
        rsa_vp1(k->n, k->n_len, candidate, power);
